    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d59">

                <pb facs="0142" n="114" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v14p1/pg114"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">293.1111/11–752: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 59<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the
                        Embassy in India</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d59-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1952-11-07T13:51:00-05:00">November 7, 1952—1:51
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1367. With ref Deptel 2802 Oct 21 to London rptd New Delhi 1177 Hong Kong 1470
                    Ottawa 77<anchor n="2" xml:id="d59-f2"/> pls ask GOI request Raghavan present
                    humanitarian appeal Peiping auths behalf Amers and other fon natls under arrest
                    Commie China along lines reftel. You shld stress matter more urgent than ever
                    with onset winter, situation of many undoubtedly critical, at least three Amers
                    having died in prison or as result imprisonment.</p>
                <p>You may inform GOI it is this govt’s understanding Brit Govt wld desire
                    Commonwealth natls in similar situation that of Amers be included in appeal, wld
                    prefer Brit Chargé Lamb Peiping concert with Raghavan if GOI agreeable, and will
                    so inform Lamb. In either case Lamb can give Raghavan current info any time re
                    nr and identity Amers and Commonwealth natls under arrest.</p>
                <pb facs="0143" n="115" xml:id="pg115"/>
                <p>Canadian Emb has informed Dept Canadian Govt will be ready ask its HC New Delhi
                    approach GOI if such action appears appropriate.</p>
                <p>Pls keep Dept informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bruce</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d59-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d59-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to London, Ottawa, and Hong Kong.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d59-f2" n="2" xml:id="d59-f2-content">
                <p>This telegram stated that the Department expected to ask the Indian Government to
                    request Raghavan to appeal to the Peking authorities on behalf of the imprisoned
                    Americans on humanitarian grounds, stressing concern that they be enabled to
                    have warm bedding and clothing, vitamins, and any needed medicine.
                    (293.1111/10–2152)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
